================================================================================
  Lead game server installed under /usr/local/lead

  The post-install step has already (best effort):
    * created the dedicated 'lead' user/group (home = /usr/local/lead)
    * built the in-tree symlinks + runtime dirs
    * autodiscovered this host's IP and wrote it as bind_ip in the core configs
    * enabled & started MariaDB and created the databases + migrations
    * enabled the service (lead_enable=YES)

  Review the autodetected address (and DB credentials) if needed - the core
  configs are @config files, preserved across upgrades:

      /usr/local/lead/auth/CONFIG
      /usr/local/lead/channel1/game1/CONFIG   (and game2, channel99, markserver)
      /usr/local/lead/db/conf.txt

  Re-run IP autodiscovery any time the host address changes:

      /usr/local/libexec/lead/lead-configure          (or LEAD_PUBLIC_IP=x.x.x.x ...)

  Manage the server with lead-ctl (start/stop all, a single channel, or a core;
  plus a full backup). Channels 1-4 (+ channel99) are configured:

      lead-ctl start            # start everything (db, auth, mark, ch1-4, ch99)
      lead-ctl start ch2        # start ONLY channel 2
      lead-ctl stop ch4         # stop ONLY channel 4
      lead-ctl status
      lead-ctl backup           # full backup (all DBs + serverfiles) to /var/backups/lead

  Or via the rc system at boot (uses lead_channels from rc.conf, default 1 2 3 4):

      service lead start
      service lead status

  Re-run the DB bootstrap any time (idempotent; applies new migrations):

      /usr/local/libexec/lead/lead-db-setup

  Update later (downloads the matching FreeBSD/arch .pkg from the GitHub release
  and upgrades in place only if newer; --check just compares versions):

      /usr/local/libexec/lead/lead-update

  Logs live under /usr/local/lead/<core>/{syserr.txt,log/}.
================================================================================
